# SemanticScript standard-library canonical module: standard.string.

module standard.string
purpose module standard.string "Canonical standard-library module for C-string helpers."
moduleOwns standard.string "The official import path `standard.string` and this module's implementation body."
moduleDoesNotOwn standard.string "App-specific wrappers, compatibility aliases, or generated build artifacts."
invariant module standard.string "The standard module entry is this file; tests live beside it as `main.test.sem`."

exportConstant standard.string stringModuleVersionText
storage module immutable stringModuleVersionText CNullTerminatedByteString "standard.string 0.1"

exportOperation standard.string findFirstCharacterInCString
exportOperation standard.string countInitialCStringBytesInAcceptSet

# Canonical standard-library implementation body.
# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: pure-SemanticScript C-string operations
# ============================================================
#
# rationale: every operation lowers to pointer.loadByte /
#   pointer.storeByte plus math primitives. NO libc string call
#   appears in the emitted IR â€” no strlen, strcmp, strchr, strstr,
#   memcpy, etc. The point is a self-contained byte-string surface
#   that does not depend on linking libc string.h.
#
# invariant: every operation walks the input forward, stops at the
#   first NUL byte (or the explicit byteCount limit). Capacity
#   enforcement on the destination buffer is the callers responsibility
#   â€” there is no destinationCapacityBytes parameter at this layer.
#
# security: buffer-overflow risk on copy / append / duplicate ops
#   when the caller misjudges destination size. A future revision
#   will add capacity contracts; today the surface mirrors libc.
#
# timing: every op is O(byteCount).
#
# observability: no logs; consumers wrap when needed.

# Pure-module file: smoke + extended tests live in
# std/string/main.test.sem.

# section capability
# rationale: every operation in this module reads (or reads+writes)
# the memory.buffer effect channel through caller-supplied pointers;
# duplicateCStringIntoOwnedMemory additionally allocates a scratch
# buffer on the heap. The stdout / heap-free capabilities used by
# the smoke main live with the test file.
capability memoryBufferReadCapability memory.buffer read
capability memoryBufferWriteCapability memory.buffer write
capability heapAllocationCapability heap allocate

# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: <string.h>-style operations.
#
# Every operation here is implemented in pure SemanticScript using
# pointer.loadByte / pointer.storeByte + math primitives. There is NO
# libc string call â€” stringByteLength / memcpy / compareCString / etc. do not appear in
# the emitted IR as externs.
#
# Operations:
#   stringByteLength(s)                  byte count up to NUL
#   compareCString(a, b)               lex compare two C-strings
#   compareCStringPrefixBytes(a, b, n)           lex compare up to n bytes
#   findFirstCharacterInCString(s, c)               offset of first c, -1 if absent
#   findLastCharacterInCString(s, c)              offset of LAST c, -1 if absent
#   findSubstringInCString(haystack, needle)   offset of first occurrence of needle, -1 if absent
#   countInitialCStringBytesInAcceptSet(s, accept)          length of leading run of bytes in accept
#   copyCStringToDestinationBuffer(dest, src)     like strcpy: copy bytes (and NUL) from src to dest
# ============================================================

# ---- stringByteLength(s) -> byte count up to NUL ----
operation stringByteLength
input operation stringByteLength inputText CNullTerminatedByteString
output operation stringByteLength CByteCount
useCapability stringByteLength memoryBufferReadCapability
effect stringByteLength read memory.buffer
memory stringByteLength heap no
memory stringByteLength stack max 1024
async stringByteLength no
purpose operation stringByteLength "Pure-SemanticScript stringByteLength: walk bytes from s until a NUL, return the count."
invariant operation stringByteLength "Walks forward from offset 0 until the first NUL byte; returns that offset as the byte count."

label startStringByteLength
storage module immutable zeroI64 I64 0
storage module immutable oneI64 I64 1
memory stringByteLength mutable cursor I64 0
label strlenLoop
call loadCall pointer.loadByte
argument loadCall buffer COpaqueMemoryAddress inputText
argument loadCall offset CByteCount cursor
run loadCall
bind value byteValue I8 loadCall
call isNullCall math.equalI64
argument isNullCall left I64 byteValue
argument isNullCall right I64 zeroI64
run isNullCall
bind value isNull Bool isNullCall
branch if condition isNull target strlenDone
call incCall math.addI64
argument incCall left I64 cursor
argument incCall right I64 oneI64
run incCall
bind value nextCursor I64 incCall
set memory cursor nextCursor
jump target strlenLoop
label strlenDone
return value cursor

# ---- compareCString(a, b) -> 0 if equal, signed diff otherwise ----
operation compareCString
input operation compareCString leftValue CNullTerminatedByteString
input operation compareCString rightValue CNullTerminatedByteString
output operation compareCString CSignedInt32
useCapability compareCString memoryBufferReadCapability
effect compareCString read memory.buffer
memory compareCString heap no
memory compareCString stack max 1024
async compareCString no
purpose operation compareCString "Pure-SemanticScript compareCString: returns 0 on equal C-strings, signed diff of first mismatching byte otherwise."
invariant operation compareCString "Walks both strings byte-by-byte; returns at the first differing byte or at the first NUL on either side."

label startCompareCString
storage module immutable zeroI64a I64 0
storage module immutable oneI64a I64 1
memory compareCString mutable idx I64 0
label strcmpLoop
call loadACall pointer.loadByte
argument loadACall buffer COpaqueMemoryAddress leftValue
argument loadACall offset CByteCount idx
run loadACall
bind value aByte I8 loadACall
call loadBCall pointer.loadByte
argument loadBCall buffer COpaqueMemoryAddress rightValue
argument loadBCall offset CByteCount idx
run loadBCall
bind value bByte I8 loadBCall
call diffCall math.subtractI64
argument diffCall left I64 aByte
argument diffCall right I64 bByte
run diffCall
bind value diff I64 diffCall
call diffNonzeroCall math.notEqualI64
argument diffNonzeroCall left I64 diff
argument diffNonzeroCall right I64 zeroI64a
run diffNonzeroCall
bind value diffNonzero Bool diffNonzeroCall
branch if condition diffNonzero target strcmpReturnDiff
call atEndCall math.equalI64
argument atEndCall left I64 aByte
argument atEndCall right I64 zeroI64a
run atEndCall
bind value atEnd Bool atEndCall
branch if condition atEnd target strcmpReturnEqual
call incIdxCall math.addI64
argument incIdxCall left I64 idx
argument incIdxCall right I64 oneI64a
run incIdxCall
bind value nextIdx I64 incIdxCall
set memory idx nextIdx
jump target strcmpLoop
label strcmpReturnDiff
return value diff
label strcmpReturnEqual
return value zeroI64a

# ---- compareCStringPrefixBytes(a, b, n) -> like compareCString but max n bytes ----
operation compareCStringPrefixBytes
input operation compareCStringPrefixBytes leftValue CNullTerminatedByteString
input operation compareCStringPrefixBytes rightValue CNullTerminatedByteString
input operation compareCStringPrefixBytes maxByteCount CByteCount
output operation compareCStringPrefixBytes CSignedInt32
useCapability compareCStringPrefixBytes memoryBufferReadCapability
effect compareCStringPrefixBytes read memory.buffer
memory compareCStringPrefixBytes heap no
memory compareCStringPrefixBytes stack max 1024
async compareCStringPrefixBytes no
purpose operation compareCStringPrefixBytes "Pure-SemanticScript compareCStringPrefixBytes: compare up to n bytes of a and b. Returns 0 if equal-in-first-n-or-both-NUL, signed diff at first mismatch, 0 if n==0."
invariant operation compareCStringPrefixBytes "At most maxByteCount bytes inspected; equality on the prefix yields 0 even if the full strings differ beyond."

label startCompareCStringPrefixBytes
storage module immutable zeroI64b I64 0
storage module immutable oneI64b I64 1
memory compareCStringPrefixBytes mutable nidx I64 0
label strncmpLoop
call nLimitCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
argument nLimitCall left I64 nidx
argument nLimitCall right I64 maxByteCount
run nLimitCall
bind value nReached Bool nLimitCall
branch if condition nReached target strncmpReturnEqual
call loadAnCall pointer.loadByte
argument loadAnCall buffer COpaqueMemoryAddress leftValue
argument loadAnCall offset CByteCount nidx
run loadAnCall
bind value anByte I8 loadAnCall
call loadBnCall pointer.loadByte
argument loadBnCall buffer COpaqueMemoryAddress rightValue
argument loadBnCall offset CByteCount nidx
run loadBnCall
bind value bnByte I8 loadBnCall
call ndiffCall math.subtractI64
argument ndiffCall left I64 anByte
argument ndiffCall right I64 bnByte
run ndiffCall
bind value ndiff I64 ndiffCall
call ndiffNzCall math.notEqualI64
argument ndiffNzCall left I64 ndiff
argument ndiffNzCall right I64 zeroI64b
run ndiffNzCall
bind value ndiffNz Bool ndiffNzCall
branch if condition ndiffNz target strncmpReturnDiff
call nEndCall math.equalI64
argument nEndCall left I64 anByte
argument nEndCall right I64 zeroI64b
run nEndCall
bind value nEnd Bool nEndCall
branch if condition nEnd target strncmpReturnEqual
call nIncCall math.addI64
argument nIncCall left I64 nidx
argument nIncCall right I64 oneI64b
run nIncCall
bind value nNext I64 nIncCall
set memory nidx nNext
jump target strncmpLoop
label strncmpReturnDiff
return value ndiff
label strncmpReturnEqual
return value zeroI64b

